---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Typography
description: The typefaces, the type roles that set every piece of text, and the scale they are built from. Each specimen is set with its own tokens.
---

{#
  Built from _data/styles.js. Specimens are set with the tokens' CSS variables,
  so they render exactly as the roles do in product code.
#}

<p>
  Set text with a <strong>type role</strong>. A role bundles a family, size,
  weight, line height, and letter spacing that belong together, as five
  variables that share a prefix:
</p>

<pre><code>.card-title {
  font-family: var(--qds-semantic-typography-title-font-family);
  font-size: var(--qds-semantic-typography-title-font-size);
  font-weight: var(--qds-semantic-typography-title-font-weight);
  line-height: var(--qds-semantic-typography-title-line-height);
  letter-spacing: var(--qds-semantic-typography-title-letter-spacing);
}</code></pre>

<p>
  In Figma, each role is a text style in the
  <a href="{{ site.figma.tokens }}" rel="noopener">Quieto Tokens</a> file, with
  its family, size, and weight bound to variables.
</p>

<h2>Type roles</h2>

<ol class="type-roles">
  {% for role in styles.typography.roles %}
    <li class="type-role">
      <p
        class="type-role__specimen"
        style="font-family: var(--{{ role.prefix }}-font-family); font-size: var(--{{ role.prefix }}-font-size); font-weight: var(--{{ role.prefix }}-font-weight); line-height: var(--{{ role.prefix }}-line-height); letter-spacing: var(--{{ role.prefix }}-letter-spacing);"
      >{% if role.role == 'data' %}--qds-semantic-color-content-default{% else %}Quiet systems scale well{% endif %}</p>
      <div class="type-role__details">
        <h3 class="type-role__name">{{ role.role | capitalize }}</h3>
        <p>{{ role.use }}</p>
        <p class="type-role__values">
          <code>{{ role.fontSize }}</code> · weight <code>{{ role.fontWeight }}</code> · line height
          <code>{{ role.lineHeight }}</code> · <code>--{{ role.prefix }}-*</code>
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>
  {% endfor %}
</ol>

<h2>Typefaces</h2>

<p>
  Three families. <strong>The tokens name the faces but do not load them</strong>:
  load Inter and JetBrains Mono in your app, or each falls back to the system
  face listed after it. This site does not load them, so what you see here is
  the fallback.
</p>

<ul class="typefaces">
  {% for family in styles.typography.families %}
    <li class="typeface">
      <p class="typeface__specimen" style="font-family: var(--{{ family.name }})">Aa Bb Cc 0123</p>
      <p class="typeface__name"><strong>{{ family.step | capitalize }}</strong> <code>--{{ family.name }}</code></p>
      <p class="typeface__stack"><code>{{ family.value }}</code></p>
    </li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>

<h2>Size scale</h2>

<p>The primitive sizes the roles draw from. Use a role in product code; reach for a step directly only when building a new one.</p>

<ol class="type-scale">
  {% for size in styles.typography.sizes | reverse %}
    <li class="type-scale__step">
      <span class="type-scale__sample" style="font-size: var(--{{ size.name }})">Ag</span>
      <span class="type-scale__label">{{ size.step }}</span>
      <code>{{ size.value }}</code>
    </li>
  {% endfor %}
</ol>

<h2>Weights</h2>

<ul class="type-weights">
  {% for weight in styles.typography.weights %}
    <li style="font-weight: var(--{{ weight.name }})">
      {{ weight.step | capitalize }} <code>{{ weight.value }}</code>
    </li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>
